      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When the entire operating system and core architecture are failing to boot or run, it suggests a deeper, systemic problem beyond a simple component failure. This kind of persistent, fatal error across all attempts points toward a critical incompatibility or a failure in the fundamental bootloader or firmware. At this stage, the only viable path forward is often a complete wipe and fresh installation, or if the motherboard itself is compromised, a total system replacement.",
      "source": "target",
